[
  {
    "sha": "a96191862cedf973c07079973540974032d0544d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGE5NjE5MTg2MmNlZGY5NzNjMDcwNzk5NzM1NDA5NzQwMzJkMDU0NGQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T09:07:39Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T09:07:39Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(wire): a tangent arc lead-in and lead-out\n\nWire Contour takes an opt-in tangent arc lead (`lead_arc_radius`, mm)\nnext to the straight lead, which stays the default. The lead circle\ntouches the path at the seam on the waste side; a tangent straight from\nthe start hole and an arc enter the path in its own direction, and the\nmirror leaves it. A radius not over the kerf offset, a hole inside the\nlead circle and a lead nearer the profile than the kerf offset are\nrefused by name, and so is the arc lead beside an open run, tabs,\nskims, a taper, a burnout, a 4-axis cut, an exit pick or a model's\nprofile. Project file (serde default), MCP field, UI row and the\ncamcraft-mcp skill row follow.\n\nRefs #3937\nFixes #3991\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
